        <p class="door-card__row door-card__row--watch"><span>Watch out</span>{item.watch}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="gulf">Gulf: fastest start, weakest protection</h2>

  <p>
    Gulf health authorities, such as the Dubai Health Authority, first check your degree and experience letters through a verification company called DataFlow, and then you sit the authority's licensing exam. DataFlow's DHA page lists a nurse package at AED 935 with a report in 15 to 24 working days, and says the exam is booked through Prometric at USD 220 to 280. Fees change, so confirm them on the authority's own page.
  </p>

  <p>
    On experience, one consultancy report from June 2026 says the UAE framework sets no post-qualification experience rule for entry-grade registered nurses, and it does not say when the change took effect. Many employers still ask for ward experience, so read the listing and ask the authority.
  </p>

  <p>
    India has required emigration clearance for nurses going to 18 "emigration check required" countries since 31 May 2015. The Ministry of External Affairs first said recruitment would be restricted to state-run agencies, and an undated Indian embassy page says the rule covers both government and private agents, with the foreign employer registered on eMigrate. Check the current list, the agent and the employer on eMigrate before you pay anything.
  </p>

  <p>
    An illustration, not an offer: if you save AED 2,500 a month on a two-year contract, you leave with AED 60,000 before flights and any fee an agent charged. A fee above the legal limit, or a contract you must repay if you leave early, can cut that sharply.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Why nurses choose the Gulf</div>
      <ul>
        <li>One recruiter-site estimate shows AED 6,000 to 10,000 a month at 2 to 5 years of experience.</li>
        <li>The same page says most nurse packages cover housing or an allowance, listed at about AED 2,000 to 5,000 a month, so the cash you save can be higher.</li>
        <li>The route is usually shorter than the UK or US routes, but each country has its own exam and rules.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">What to check first</div>
      <ul>
        <li>The contract in writing: basic pay, housing, transport, leave and notice.</li>
        <li>That no agent charges more than the legal limit, and that every payment has a receipt.</li>
        <li>That you will not be asked to repay hiring costs if you leave early.</li>
        <li>What your plan is for year three, because the stay ends with the contract.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="pay-vs-india">Pay abroad next to pay in India</h2>

  <p>
    The numbers come from different kinds of sources, so compare direction and not decimals.
  </p>

